Check 1 — "packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> [<file> ...] checks every file named in order and prints <file>:<line>: <error> for each bad row, as for one file before"
Run `node $CLI $T/good1.jsonl $T/bad.jsonl $T/good2.jsonl`, then `cp $T/bad.jsonl $T/bad2.jsonl` and `node $CLI $T/bad.jsonl $T/bad2.jsonl`, and also `node $CLI $T/bad.jsonl` alone.
